<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_EcatDiagWrapper" Id="{ae68027c-9136-4dab-b887-f964a869ea04}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_EcatDiagWrapper
(*
    FB_EcatDiagWrapper - one EtherCAT bus verdict for one master, condensed from the
    two underlying diagnostic blocks.

    PURPOSE
        Bundle the two EtherCAT diagnostic blocks a program needs, so a caller
        gets a whole-bus verdict from a single instance and a single call.
        fbEtherCATFrameDiag condenses the master's first-frame WcState word into
        bFrameWcStateOK, which this block publishes as bAllFrameWcStatesOK.
        fbEtherCATDiag then takes that flag together with the master's slave
        counts and device state and produces the deep diagnostic: bEtherCATOK
        plus the separate bFrameWcStateError / bSlaveCountError /
        bMasterDevStateError flags, the decoded stMasterDevState structure, and
        - while a fault is being investigated - a per-slave JSON record on the
        shared logger. bBusy, bError and iErrorID report the state of that inner
        diagnostic.

    USAGE
        Declare one instance in a GVL and call it every PLC cycle. The block has
        no VAR_INPUT: everything it needs it reads through its own linked AT %I*
        variables, so the caller passes nothing and the wiring lives in the
        declaration below. Every link points at the EtherCAT master's IO and
        hard-codes the master name "Device 1 (EtherCAT)"; a project whose master
        device carries another name must retarget all six TcLinkTo pragmas, or
        the block reads zeros and reports a slave-count error against a healthy
        bus. Links required: Inputs^Frm1WcState (frame WcState word),
        Inputs^SlaveCount and InfoData^CfgSlaveCount (found vs configured slave
        count), Inputs^DevState (master device state) and InfoData^DevId /
        InfoData^AmsNetId (the master's identity).
        Wiring side effects worth knowing:
        - arrEcMasterNetId is mandatory. F_CreateAmsNetId turns it into
          sEcMasterNetId, and while that is empty or '0.0.0.0.0.0' the inner
          diagnostic sets bError with iErrorID = 7 instead of starting, so a
          missed NetId link surfaces as a latched bError rather than as silence.
        - sIPCNetID is passed as '' (local IPC) and eSubSystem is not forwarded,
          so the inner diagnostic keeps its own E_Subsystem.FIELDBUS default and
          logs under the fieldbus subsystem.
        - tTimeout is fixed at T#5s here for every ADS request the inner
          diagnostic issues. Because wReqZeroMask and tTimeout are internal
          declarations rather than inputs, a project that needs a different
          frame mask or ADS timeout must change them in this block.
        The masked frame check is combinational, so bAllFrameWcStatesOK follows
        the frame word in the same cycle; the deeper verdict in bEtherCATOK comes
        from the inner state machine, which only sweeps the bus when one of the
        observed inputs changes.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Give a program one instance and one call for EtherCAT diagnostics,
          instead of instantiating and plumbing the two lower-level blocks.
        - Keep the raw master IO links in a single place, so the IO mapping of a
          bus is reviewable in one declaration rather than at every call site.
        - Expose the frame, slave-count and master-device-state faults as
          separate flags, so a caller or EPICS record can react to the kind of
          fault rather than to a single opaque "bus not OK".
        - Hand the deep diagnostic's per-slave detail to the shared logger, so a
          bus failure leaves a diagnosable record without the caller collecting
          it.

    HISTORY
        2020-03-15 / Alex Wallace
            Function block added with the BI EtherCAT diagnostics example,
            wrapping FB_EtherCATFrameDiag and FB_EtherCATDiag.
        2020-03-15 / Alex Wallace
            Same-day follow-ups: TcLinkTo paths corrected for the master inputs,
            and the extra "fast frame" input removed again.
        2020-03-25 / Alex Wallace
            Slave-info arrays widened from ARRAY [0..3] to ARRAY [0..ESC_MAX_PORTS]
            so the diagnostic covers every ESC port.
        2021-11-02 / K Lauer
            Style pass: pre-commit run --all-files (leading tabs, trailing
            whitespace); no logic change.
        2023-05-22 / Jakob Sagatowski
            Removed the "Write product version in files" flag from the projects.
        2026-11-28 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header comment; declaration and implementation bodies
            unchanged, existing inline declaration comments kept (audit finding
            #83, convention conv_321640e095c0).

    NOTE
        The two VAR_IN_OUT arrays of FB_EtherCATDiag are fed from this block's own
        arrDiagSlaveInfo / arrDiagSlaveInfoScanned buffers, sized ESC_MAX_PORTS, so
        the per-slave diagnostic data stays inside this instance and is not
        published to the caller; it reaches consumers only through the logger.
*)
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    bAllFrameWcStatesOK		: BOOL;				// all frames are OK
    bEtherCATOK				: BOOL;				// no problem on EtherCAT
    bFrameWcStateError		: BOOL;				// at least one fram with error
    bSlaveCountError		: BOOL;				// EtherCAT slave count mismatch (# of cfg slaves <> # of found slaves)
    bMasterDevStateError	: BOOL;				// EtherCAT master device state signals error
    stMasterDevState		: ST_EcMasterDevState; // device state split to a structure
    bBusy					: BOOL;				// diagnostic FB is busy
    bError					: BOOL;				// diagnostic FB has an error
    iErrorID				: UDINT;			// error ID of diagnostic FB
END_VAR
VAR

    (* ******************* EtherCAT Frame ***************************** *)
    fbEtherCATFrameDiag		: FB_EtherCATFrameDiag; // frame diagnostic
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^Inputs^Frm1WcState'}
    wFrmXWcState AT %I*		: WORD; 			// link to task related ethercat frame state (Frm1WcState)
    wReqZeroMask			: WORD := 16#FFFF; 	// clear bit to ignore datagram error of Frm1WcState
    bFrameWcStateOK			: BOOL;				// this frame is OK

    (* ******************* EtherCAT Diag ***************************** *)
    fbEtherCATDiag			: FB_EtherCATDiag;	// deep EtherCAT diagnostic

    (* cyclic variables from EtherCAT Master *)
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^Inputs^SlaveCount'}
    nEcMasterSlaveCount AT %I* 	: UINT;			// link to SlaveCount of EtherCAT Master (Inputs)
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^Inputs^DevState'}
    nEcMasterDevState AT %I* 	: UINT;			// link to DevState of EtherCAT Master (Inputs)
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^InfoData^DevId'}
    nEcMasterDeviceId AT %I*	: UINT;			// link to DevID of EtherCAT Master (InfoData)
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^InfoData^AmsNetId'}
    arrEcMasterNetId AT %I* 	: T_AmsNetIdArr;// link to NetID of EtherCAT Master (InfoData)
    sEcMasterNetId  			: T_AmsNetId := '';
    {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := 'TIID^Device 1 (EtherCAT)^InfoData^CfgSlaveCount'}
    nEcMasterSlaveCountCfg AT %I* 	: UINT;		// link to CfgSlaveCount of EtherCAT Master (InfoData)

    (* general variables *)
    arrDiagSlaveInfo 			: ARRAY [0..ESC_MAX_PORTS] OF ST_SlaveStateInfo;		// read in info of configured EtherCAT slaves
    arrDiagSlaveInfoScanned		: ARRAY [0..ESC_MAX_PORTS] OF ST_SlaveStateInfoScanned; // read in info of scanned EtherCAT slaves
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[
(*************************************** Frame Diag *********************************************)
fbEtherCATFrameDiag(
    wFrmXWcState 	:= wFrmXWcState,
    wReqZeroMask 	:= wReqZeroMask,
    bFrameWcStateOK	=> bFrameWcStateOK
);
bAllFrameWcStatesOK := bFrameWcStateOK;

(*************************************** EtherCAT Diag *********************************************)
(* generate Net Id *)
sEcMasterNetId := F_CreateAmsNetId(nIds := arrEcMasterNetId);
fbEtherCATDiag(
    sIPCNetID			:= '',
    sMasterNetID		:= sEcMasterNetId,
    nMasterDevID		:= nEcMasterDeviceId,
    nSlaveCount			:= nEcMasterSlaveCount,
    nSlaveCountCfg		:= nEcMasterSlaveCountCfg,
    nMasterDevState		:= nEcMasterDevState,
    bAllFrameWcStatesOK	:= bAllFrameWcStatesOK,
    tTimeout			:= T#5s,
    arrDiagSlaveInfo	:= arrDiagSlaveInfo,
    arrDiagSlaveInfoScanned	:= arrDiagSlaveInfoScanned,
    bEtherCATOK			=> bEtherCATOK,
    bFrameWcStateError	=> bFrameWcStateError,
    bSlaveCountError	=> bSlaveCountError,
    bMasterDevStateError=> bMasterDevStateError,
    stMasterDevState	=> stMasterDevState,
    bBusy				=> bBusy,
    bError				=> bError,
    iErrorID			=> iErrorID
);
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>